      "body": "## Purpose\n\nA parser that identifies reasoning or tool-call boundaries by token ID can miss a boundary emitted as ordinary vocabulary tokens, even when the decoded text looks correct. Explain this contract for custom grammars and show XGrammar token-level structural tags. Qwen3 is the concrete example. Related to #58105.\n\nThe warning is under Reasoning Outputs. Tool Calling links to it from Automatic Function Calling, before the model-specific sections. Runtime parsing is unchanged.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Run changed-file pre-commit hooks.\n- Render the warning and check the heading, cross-reference anchor, and JSON examples.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- At `4354a7b487`, all applicable changed-file pre-commit hooks passed, including markdownlint and typos. Commit hooks and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Markdown rendering confirmed the warning, Reasoning Outputs nesting, and cross-reference anchor. Both JSON examples parse. A full MkDocs site build was not run.\n- Earlier CPU reproduction: 24 streaming parser cases, 8 text EBNF cases, and 8 token-constrained structural-tag cases passed. This used main at `d421a2e8fc0fd17c46c131d5c0884af5cf075fca`, XGrammar 0.2.7, and the Qwen3.6 tokenizer at `95a723d08a9490559dae23d0cff1d9466213d989`. Those results predate this documentation update; runtime and GPU tests were not rerun.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex generated the documentation and ran the checks.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] Purpose and related issue.\n- [x] Test plan and commands.\n- [x] Test results and validation limits.\n- [x] Documentation update.\n</details>\n",
